    "source_excerpt": "Spironolactone passes into breast milk in small amounts. These amounts are not expected to cause side effects in most nursing infants. If you suspect the baby has any symptoms (such as drowsiness or trouble feeding), contact the child’s healthcare provider. Be sure to talk to your healthcare provider about all your breastfeeding questions."
